<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Reserve Bank of India">
  <data key="d0">Reserve Bank of India</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Reserve Bank of India is the central bank of India, responsible for regulating the country's monetary policy and overseeing the financial system.&lt;SEP&gt;The central bank of India, responsible for regulating the country's financial system, including issuing directives on interest rates and managing deposit accounts.&lt;SEP&gt;The central banking institution of India that regulates the financial system, including interest rates set by banks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reserve Bank of India is the central banking institution of India, which regulates the banking sector and ensures financial stability.&lt;SEP&gt;The central bank of India, which issues regulatory mandates that financial institutions must adhere to.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Reserve Bank of India</data>
</node>
<node id="Door Step Banking">
  <data key="d0">Door Step Banking</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Door Step Banking refers to a banking service model where banks provide various services at the customer's location, aimed at facilitating access for senior citizens and differently-abled individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unity Bank">
  <data key="d0">Unity Bank</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Unity Bank is a financial institution that offers banking services to individuals and businesses, including a scheme for Door Step Banking.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Senior Citizens">
  <data key="d0">Senior Citizens</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Senior Citizens refers to individuals who are aged 60 years and older, often targeted for specific banking services to accommodate their needs.&lt;SEP&gt;A demographic category of individuals who are typically aged 65 and above and may have specific banking needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Senior Citizens</data>
</node>
<node id="Differently-Abled">
  <data key="d0">Differently-Abled</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Differently-Abled refers to individuals with physical or mental disabilities, who are afforded special banking services to ensure accessibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KYC Document">
  <data key="d0">KYC Document</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">KYC Document refers to documents required for 'Know Your Customer' compliance, necessary for identity verification in financial transactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cash Management Vendor">
  <data key="d0">Cash Management Vendor</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A Cash Management Vendor is a third-party service provider that manages cash logistics and operations for banks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Banking Correspondents">
  <data key="d0">Banking Correspondents</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Banking Correspondents are individuals or entities that act as representatives for banks to provide services, often in remote areas.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TPIN">
  <data key="d0">TPIN</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TPIN refers to Transaction Personal Identification Number, a security measure used to authenticate service requests in banking.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Doorstep Banking Services">
  <data key="d0">Doorstep Banking Services</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Doorstep Banking Services refer to the various banking services provided directly at the customer's location, as stated in the RBI guidelines, aimed at enhancing convenience for individuals unable to access traditional banking setups.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Charges">
  <data key="d0">Service Charges</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Service Charges refer to the fees that may be levied by Unity Bank for the Door Step Banking services, which can vary based on different account types or transaction sizes.&lt;SEP&gt;Service charges are fees levied by the bank for availing various services, which are detailed in leaflets provided to customers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Service Charges</data>
</node>
<node id="Request for Door-Step Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Request for Door-Step Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Request for Door-Step Delivery denotes the customer's initiation of a service request for the Door Step Banking services, which can be made through various channels.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bank Service Savings Per Instance">
  <data key="d0">Bank Service Savings Per Instance</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A table outlining the savings allowable for various banking services designed for individuals, senior citizens, and differently abled customers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
