</node>
<node id="Cash Pickup">
  <data key="d0">Cash Pickup</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of banking service that allows customers to withdraw cash from a specified location.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cash Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Cash Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of banking service where cash is delivered directly to the customer's location.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Differently Abled Customers">
  <data key="d0">Differently Abled Customers</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A demographic category of individuals with disabilities that may affect their ability to access standard banking services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Current Account Customers">
  <data key="d0">Current Account Customers</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals who hold current accounts in banks, which are primarily used for daily transactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="tb-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-0001">
  <data key="d0">tb-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-0001</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">[Table Name]bank_service_savings_per_instance

The table outlines the savings allowable per instance for various banking services specifically designed for individuals, senior citizens, and differently abled customers. It consists of four columns: 'Type of service', 'Savings (individuals)', 'Senior Citizen / Differently Abled', and 'Current Account Customers'. There are three types of services listed, namely 'Cash Pickup' and 'Cash Delivery', each with specified maximum savings that can be accessed per instance by different customer categories. For both 'Cash Pickup' and 'Cash Delivery', the maximum savings allowed for individuals and senior citizens/differently abled customers is 20,000, while current account customers can access up to 5 lacs per instance. The table suggests a straightforward structure for understanding the limits placed on different financial transactions catered to specific demographics, illustrating a potential disparity in service offerings based on customer classification. The footnote indicates that these values are subject to change based on the bank's policies, emphasizing that the information may evolve over time. Overall, this table serves as a reference point for potential customers to understand the financial boundaries associated with these banking services.

[Table Footnotes]# Subject to change from time to time as per banks policy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
