</node>
<node id="Depositors">
  <data key="d0">Depositors</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals or entities who place funds into deposit accounts in banks, forming a major stakeholder group in the banking system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deposit Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Deposit Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Financial accounts where depositors place their money with banks, which can be subject to interest rates and other operational conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Financial System">
  <data key="d0">Financial System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An economic framework comprising institutions, markets, instruments, and rules that facilitate the transfer of money and offer financial services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customers">
  <data key="d0">Customers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals or entities who utilize banking services and are recipients of the rights and services outlined in the deposit policy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bank">
  <data key="d0">Bank</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bank is a financial institution that plays a crucial role in the economy by offering a variety of banking products and services. It primarily focuses on managing financial accounts, which include demand and term deposits, and provides various deposit products tailored to meet customer needs. The institution accepts deposits from customers and pays interest on these funds, ensuring adherence to applicable laws and guidelines to facilitate smooth account operations.

Additionally, the Bank offers an array of services beyond deposit accounts, such as providing debit cards, mobile banking, and loans. It is responsible for processing claims, managing term deposits, and establishing policies regarding withdrawals and penalties. Furthermore, the Bank serves its customers not just with financial transactions but also by offering financial guidance and assistance in navigating banking services.

A specific example of a banking entity is Unity Small Finance Bank Ltd., which caters to the financial services sector by providing account management and staff benefits among its offerings. This reinforces the diverse nature of banks in their operational capacity and the essential roles they play in individual financial management and broader economic systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704172</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RBI">
  <data key="d0">RBI</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Reserve Bank of India, which issues guidelines and regulations related to banking and financial operations in India.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reserve Bank of India, which sets regulations, including minimum tenor requirements for term deposits and interest rates applicable.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) is the central banking institution of India, responsible for regulating the issue and supply of the Indian rupee.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reserve Bank of India is the central bank of India responsible for regulating the country's monetary policy and overseeing banking operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reserve Bank of India, which sets regulations that Unity Small Finance Bank aims to comply with in its policy updates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account (BSBDA)">
  <data key="d0">Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account (BSBDA)</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of savings account offered by banks adhering to guidelines specified by the RBI, accessible to individuals for basic banking needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Savings Account">
  <data key="d0">Savings Account</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A form of demand deposit with restrictions on the number of withdrawals that can be made during a specific period.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of bank account that earns interest on the deposited funds and allows for regular withdrawals.&lt;SEP&gt;A common bank account that earns interest on the deposit amount, typically lower than that of a term deposit, and used for withdrawing funds conveniently.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Current Account">
  <data key="d0">Current Account</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A form of demand deposit that allows for unlimited withdrawals up to a specific amount, suitable for businesses and individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;A Current Account is a bank account designed for frequent transactions and does not typically earn interest, intended for businesses and individuals managing cash flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Term Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Term Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Deposits accepted by the Bank for a fixed period, which may include recurring, short-term, and fixed deposits.&lt;SEP&gt;Deposits held for a fixed term at a specified interest rate, decided by the bank according to regulatory guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Know Your Customer (KYC)">
  <data key="d0">Know Your Customer (KYC)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A regulatory process that banks must follow to verify the identity of their clients before opening accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cash Credit (CC)">
  <data key="d0">Cash Credit (CC)</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A facility extended by banks allowing borrowers to withdraw funds from their account up to a specified limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Overdraft (OD)">
  <data key="d0">Overdraft (OD)</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">An arrangement where a bank allows a customer to withdraw more money than is available in their account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Permanent Account Number (PAN)">
  <data key="d0">Permanent Account Number (PAN)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A unique identification number issued to all taxpayers in India, required for financial transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;A unique identifier issued by the government for individuals under the Indian tax system, required in the personal details section of the form.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-drawing-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minimum Average Balance">
  <data key="d0">Minimum Average Balance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The least amount that account holders must maintain in their accounts to avoid penalties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bulk Deposit">
  <data key="d0">Bulk Deposit</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Single Rupee term deposits amounting to three crore and above, requiring specific conditions for opening.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-callable deposits">
  <data key="d0">Non-callable deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Single Rupee term deposits of above one crore where premature withdrawal is not permitted under any circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HUF">
  <data key="d0">HUF</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A Hindu Undivided Family, a legal entity for taxation and financial purposes, often used in India.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Limited Liability Partnership">
  <data key="d0">Limited Liability Partnership</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A business structure in which partners have limited liabilities, combining elements of partnerships and corporations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Debit Card">
  <data key="d0">Debit Card</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A Debit Card is a card issued by the Bank to customers with Savings or Current Accounts, allowing them to access their funds electronically.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mobile Banking">
  <data key="d0">Mobile Banking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mobile Banking is a service provided by the Bank that enables customers to conduct banking transactions using mobile devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="WhatsApp Banking">
  <data key="d0">WhatsApp Banking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">WhatsApp Banking is a banking service offered by the Bank that allows customers to interact and perform banking transactions via the WhatsApp messaging platform.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internet Banking">
  <data key="d0">Internet Banking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Internet Banking is a service that allows customers to manage their bank accounts and perform transactions online through the Bank's website.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ATM Network">
  <data key="d0">ATM Network</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The ATM Network includes both the Bank's own ATMs and those of other banks, allowing customers to withdraw cash and perform banking transactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NEFT">
  <data key="d0">NEFT</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">NEFT (National Electronic Funds Transfer) is an electronic payment system that facilitates the transfer of funds between banks in India, offered as a service by the Bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RTGS">
  <data key="d0">RTGS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">RTGS (Real Time Gross Settlement) is a payment system that enables the electronic transfer of funds in real time, provided by the Bank as part of its banking services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statement of Account">
  <data key="d0">Statement of Account</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A Statement of Account is a monthly report provided by the Bank to account holders detailing the transactions and balances in their accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Savings Bank Account">
  <data key="d0">Savings Bank Account</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A Savings Bank Account is a type of bank account that allows individuals to deposit and withdraw money while earning interest.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minor">
  <data key="d0">Minor</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A Minor is an individual under the age of legal adulthood, who can open and operate a savings account with the consent of a guardian.&lt;SEP&gt;A minor refers to an individual under the legal age of adulthood, which impacts their ability to open bank accounts independently without a guardian.&lt;SEP&gt;The minor refers to individuals under the legal age of adulthood, whose KYC data needs to be processed and managed using the BIDMS system at Unity Small Finance Bank.&lt;SEP&gt;Minor is an individual who has not yet reached the age of majority, and whose account may require changes upon reaching this age.&lt;SEP&gt;An identification indicating that the form is created for a minor applicant, as specified in the form's 'Name/title' field.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-drawing-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian">
  <data key="d0">Guardian</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A person appointed to care for and manage the property and affairs of another person, particularly those with disabilities or under legal guardianship.&lt;SEP&gt;A Guardian is a person who has the legal authority to act on behalf of a minor in the context of financial and legal decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;A guardian is a person appointed to care for and make decisions on behalf of someone unable to do so, particularly minors and disabled individuals in banking contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;A guardian is a person appointed by the District Courts or Collectors of Districts to manage the affairs of a mentally ill person under the Mental Health Act, 1987.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Account">
  <data key="d0">Joint Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Joint Account is a bank account shared by two or more individuals, allowing them to manage finances together.&lt;SEP&gt;A joint account is an account shared by two or more persons, allowing them to manage finances together, subject to specific approval and documentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power of Attorney">
  <data key="d0">Power of Attorney</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Power of Attorney is a legal document that allows one person to act on behalf of another in financial or legal matters.&lt;SEP&gt;A Power of Attorney (POA) is a legal document that allows one person to act on behalf of another, typically for significant or legal transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Power of Attorney (POA) is a legal document that grants one person the authority to act on behalf of another in legal or financial decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nomination">
  <data key="d0">Nomination</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Nomination is a facility allowing account holders to designate a person who will receive the account balance in case of the account holder's passing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Depositor">
  <data key="d0">Depositor</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A person who deposits money into a bank account and may nominate another individual to receive the funds in specific circumstances.&lt;SEP&gt;The individual who holds a term deposit account with the bank, which can be subject to terms regarding withdrawal and interest payout upon maturity or death.&lt;SEP&gt;A depositor is an individual who places funds into a bank account and may also be eligible to claim amounts from inoperative accounts or unclaimed deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nominee">
  <data key="d0">Nominee</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual named by the depositor who will receive the deposited amount on behalf of a minor, or in the event of the death of the depositor.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual designated to receive the benefits of a term deposit in the event of the depositor's death.&lt;SEP&gt;A nominee is an individual designated by the depositor, or legal heir, to claim the funds from a bank account upon the depositor's passing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Legal Heirs">
  <data key="d0">Legal Heirs</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals entitled by law to inherit the assets or liabilities of the deceased depositor.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals legally entitled to inherit the assets of a deceased depositor, involved in the claims process for term deposits after the depositor's death.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visually Challenged Person">
  <data key="d0">Visually Challenged Person</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual with visual impairments who may require special banking services and accommodations to access their accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transgender Person">
  <data key="d0">Transgender Person</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual who identifies as a gender different from their assigned gender at birth and is recognized as 'Third Gender' for banking purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;A transgender person is an individual who identifies as a gender that is different from their biological sex and is recognized as 'Third Gender' for banking purposes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Resident Individual">
  <data key="d0">Non-Resident Individual</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals residing outside their country of citizenship, who may hold bank accounts subject to specific regulatory guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Master Policy on Customer Service">
  <data key="d0">Master Policy on Customer Service</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A comprehensive document outlining the policies and guidelines related to customer service and account operations provided by the Bank.&lt;SEP&gt;A foundational document that outlines the various policies and measures employed by the bank to ensure customer service and satisfaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and Multiple Disabilities Act, 1999">
  <data key="d0">National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and Multiple Disabilities Act, 1999</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An act that provides legal framework for the care and management of individuals with disabilities, allowing banking operations under specific provisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mental Health Act, 1987">
  <data key="d0">Mental Health Act, 1987</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Legislation governing the care and legal status of individuals with mental health issues, impacting the opening of bank accounts on their behalf.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mental Health Act, 1987 is a law that governs the treatment and care of mentally ill persons, ensuring better provision for their property and affairs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Account Holder">
  <data key="d0">Account Holder</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The individual who owns a deposit account with the Bank and has rights and responsibilities regarding the operation of that account.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals or entities that own an account with the bank and are involved in transactions and account management.&lt;SEP&gt;Account Holder refers to individuals authorized to operate a bank account, which can include minors and their guardians.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Illiterate Person">
  <data key="d0">Illiterate Person</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual who is unable to read or write and is subject to specific conditions when opening a bank account to safeguard interests.&lt;SEP&gt;An illiterate person in the banking context is an individual who cannot read or write and must be treated with special considerations when opening a bank account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Senior Citizen">
  <data key="d0">Senior Citizen</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A Resident Indian individual aged over 60 years eligible for higher interest rates on Fixed Deposits as per the Bank's policies.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual defined by age, generally over a certain number of years, who may be eligible for additional benefits in the context of bank services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Domestic Account">
  <data key="d0">Domestic Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Accounts held within the domestic banking system, which includes deposits subject to specific interest rates and conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Resident Ordinary Account">
  <data key="d0">Non-Resident Ordinary Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of account for non-resident individuals to manage income earned in India, which allows for interest payments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Resident External Account">
  <data key="d0">Non-Resident External Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An account for non-resident Indians to manage foreign earnings, which may also incur interest according to bank policy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interest Rate">
  <data key="d0">Interest Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The percentage at which interest is paid by the bank for deposits held in accounts, varying by account type and conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The percentage at which interest is paid on the amount deposited, defined by the bank for different types of accounts and conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recurring Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Recurring Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of term deposit where investors deposit a fixed amount regularly and earn interest at a specified rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Funds placed in a bank account subject to earning interest based on specific terms set by the bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interest Rate Card">
  <data key="d0">Interest Rate Card</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A document or digital record maintained by the bank that lists the interest rates applicable across various deposit accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Term Deposit">
  <data key="d0">Term Deposit</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A financial product offered by the bank where a sum of money is deposited for a fixed period, earning interest at a specified rate until maturity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tax Deduction Certificate">
  <data key="d0">Tax Deduction Certificate</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A document issued by the bank to a depositor, certifying the amount of tax deducted at source on interest paid or payable on term deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Form 15G/15H">
  <data key="d0">Form 15G/15H</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Declarations submitted by depositors to claim exemption from tax deduction at source, necessary for managing TDS on interest income.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Term Deposit Account">
  <data key="d0">Term Deposit Account</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The specific account set up by the depositor for managing the term deposits, which may be subject to terms regarding premature withdrawal and renewal.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Premature Withdrawal">
  <data key="d0">Premature Withdrawal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The process by which a depositor can withdraw funds from a term deposit account before the agreed maturity date, subject to specific bank policies and penalties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minimum Tenor">
  <data key="d0">Minimum Tenor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The required minimum period that a term deposit must remain active, specified by the RBI, such as seven days for NRO term deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maturity Date">
  <data key="d0">Maturity Date</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The date on which the term deposit becomes due for payment, with interest payable until this date for a depositor or their nominee.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NRE Deposits">
  <data key="d0">NRE Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">NRE (Non-Resident External) deposits are a type of bank account offered to non-resident Indians that allow them to deposit income earned outside India.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NRO Deposits">
  <data key="d0">NRO Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">NRO (Non-Resident Ordinary) deposits are bank accounts for non-resident Indians that facilitate the management of income generated in India.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scheduled Commercial Banks">
  <data key="d0">Scheduled Commercial Banks</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Scheduled Commercial Banks are banks that are included in the Second Schedule of the Reserve Bank of India Act, 1934, and are eligible for financial assistance from the Reserve Bank.&lt;SEP&gt;Scheduled Commercial Banks are banks included in the Second Schedule of the Reserve Bank of India Act and can accept deposits and provide banking services under regulatory guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Board of Directors">
  <data key="d0">Board of Directors</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Board of Directors refers to a group of individuals elected to represent shareholders and govern an organization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deposit Insurance and Credit Guarantee Corporation of India">
  <data key="d0">Deposit Insurance and Credit Guarantee Corporation of India</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">DICGC is an institution established by the Reserve Bank of India to provide deposit insurance to depositors in case of bank failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Information">
  <data key="d0">Customer Information</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer Information refers to the data collected from customers regarding their banking accounts and financial transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Customer information refers to the personal details required from individuals to process account openings, including fields like 'Customer Branch,' 'Customer Name,' 'DOB,' and 'PAN No.'</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-drawing-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unclaimed Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Unclaimed Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unclaimed Deposits are accounts that have not been operated for a specified period, leading to their transfer to the Reserve Bank of India as per regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Unclaimed deposits are funds in a bank account that have not been claimed by the depositor or their nominee/legal heir within a certain timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dormant Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Dormant Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dormant Accounts refer to accounts that have not been operated for two years, requiring a request from the customer to reactivate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inactive Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Inactive Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inactive Accounts are accounts that have not had any financial transactions for one year, necessitating notification to the account holder.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insurance Cover for Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Insurance Cover for Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insurance Cover for Deposits refers to the protection offered to depositors by the DICGC up to a specified limit in case of bank insolvency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Loans Against Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Loans Against Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Loans Against Deposits allow customers to borrow money against their term deposits, subject to specific policy conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Public">
  <data key="d0">Public</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The public refers to the members of society who are potential or current customers of the bank and are targeted for financial education and services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Legal Heir">
  <data key="d0">Legal Heir</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A legal heir is an individual entitled to inherit the assets of the deceased depositor, including any funds held in bank accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Banking Ombudsman">
  <data key="d0">Banking Ombudsman</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Banking Ombudsman is an authority appointed by the Reserve Bank of India to address and resolve complaints and grievances from bank customers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grievance Redressal Policy">
  <data key="d0">Grievance Redressal Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">This policy outlines the procedures and authorities designated by the bank to handle complaints and grievances from customers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Selling Agents">
  <data key="d0">Direct Selling Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Direct Selling Agents are individuals or entities employed by banks to market their products and services directly to consumers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Business Facilitators">
  <data key="d0">Business Facilitators</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Business Facilitators are entities or individuals that assist banks in conducting their business and service operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Business Correspondents">
  <data key="d0">Business Correspondents</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Business Correspondents are individuals or entities that help banks provide services to customers in remote or underserved areas.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inoperative Account">
  <data key="d0">Inoperative Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An inoperative account refers to a bank account that has not seen any transactions for a specific period, leading to its status as inactive, usually making the funds therein unclaimed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Awareness Campaigns">
  <data key="d0">Customer Awareness Campaigns</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">These campaigns are organized by the bank to educate the public about banking services, including the process for activating inoperative accounts and claiming unclaimed deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electronic Clearing Service">
  <data key="d0">Electronic Clearing Service</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">This method, also known as ECS, is used for effecting periodic payments through direct debits from the customer's bank account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automated Clearing House">
  <data key="d0">Automated Clearing House</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Automated Clearing House is a network used for electronically moving money between bank accounts, similar to the ECS.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stop Payment Facility">
  <data key="d0">Stop Payment Facility</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Stop Payment Facility allows depositors to instruct the bank to prevent payment on specified cheques they have issued.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standing Instructions">
  <data key="d0">Standing Instructions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Standing instructions are pre-authorized instructions given by a customer to transfer or remit funds automatically from one account to another.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Depositor(s)">
  <data key="d0">Depositor(s)</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d2">Depositor(s) may request Loans Against Deposits from banks, providing necessary documents as per bank policy.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786696706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
