<node id="Surinderpal Singh R S">
  <data key="d0">Surinderpal Singh R S</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Surinderpal Singh R S is an Executive Vice President who approved the standard operating procedures for account opening for retail customers.&lt;SEP&gt;Group Head – Branch Banking Controls at Unity Small Finance Bank, responsible for overseeing branch banking operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Surinderpal Singh R S is the Executive Vice President at Unity Small Finance Bank and the individual who approved the Standard Operating Procedure for account opening on April 29, 2023.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-005</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ponnuraj P">
  <data key="d0">Ponnuraj P</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ponnuraj P is the Head of Product &amp; Distribution who approved the standard operating procedures for account opening for retail customers.&lt;SEP&gt;Head - Product &amp; Distribution at Unity Small Finance Bank, managing the bank's products and distribution channels.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-005</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gautam Chawla">
  <data key="d0">Gautam Chawla</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Gautam Chawla is the National Head of Retail Branch Banking who approved the standard operating procedures for account opening for retail customers.&lt;SEP&gt;National Head - Retail Branch Banking at Unity Small Finance Bank, overseeing retail branch banking activities across the institution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-005</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KYC Documents">
  <data key="d0">KYC Documents</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">KYC Documents refer to 'Know Your Customer' documents required for account activation and customer verification in banking processes.&lt;SEP&gt;KYC Documents refer to the Know Your Customer documents necessary for customer identification and account opening, which include an array of officially valid documents.&lt;SEP&gt;Know Your Customer (KYC) documents are required for verifying the identity of customers when opening bank accounts or completing financial transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Documents required for 'Know Your Customer' verification to maintain account security and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Know Your Customer documents required for verifying customer identity and fulfilling regulatory requirements in banking.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aadhaar Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Aadhaar Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Aadhaar authentication is a process for verifying identity using a unique identification number assigned to residents of India, facilitating easier customer onboarding.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consumer Banking">
  <data key="d0">Consumer Banking</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Consumer banking refers to banking services offered to individual consumers rather than businesses, including savings accounts and personal loans.&lt;SEP&gt;A department within a bank focused on providing banking services to individual consumers.&lt;SEP&gt;The department responsible for the ownership and management of the Standard Operating Procedures document.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Permanent Account Number">
  <data key="d0">Permanent Account Number</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Permanent Account Number (PAN) is a unique identifier issued to individuals and entities for tax purposes in India, essential for various financial transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Permanent Account Number (PAN) is an essential documentation requirement for opening accounts at Unity Small Finance Bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enhanced Due Diligence">
  <data key="d0">Enhanced Due Diligence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD) is a rigorous process undertaken by banks to assess the risk of fraud or money laundering associated with certain customers or transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD) is a process involving additional scrutiny and monitoring of high-risk customers to prevent illegal activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Enhanced Due Diligence refers to the increased scrutiny and compliance measures in banking operations as outlined in the documentation requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD) refers to the additional scrutiny applied to customers who may present higher risks, requiring more detailed information and documentation to mitigate potential risks.&lt;SEP&gt;A comprehensive process undertaken by financial institutions, including Unity Small Finance Bank, to verify and assess the potential risks associated with a business or customer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-017</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Heads">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Heads</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster Heads are designated bank officials who must approve the opening of joint accounts with non-relatives in exceptional cases.&lt;SEP&gt;Cluster heads are managerial roles within the bank responsible for overseeing operations within a designated cluster of branches.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compliance Department">
  <data key="d0">Compliance Department</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Compliance Department ensures that the bank adheres to legal standards and internal policies, particularly regarding customer onboarding and account management.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RBI Circular">
  <data key="d0">RBI Circular</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">RBI Circular is an official document issued by the Reserve Bank of India containing regulations and updates that banks must comply with.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medium Risk Customers">
  <data key="d0">Medium Risk Customers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medium Risk Customers are individuals whose risk level in banking transactions is assessed to be medium, and whose KYC documents need periodic updates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change History">
  <data key="d0">Change History</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Change History is a record of revisions made to the banking procedures, including version updates and compliance changes, throughout its implementation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inoperative Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Inoperative Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inoperative Accounts refer to banking accounts that have not had any activity for a specified period, requiring specific procedures for activation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scheme Code Change">
  <data key="d0">Scheme Code Change</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scheme Code Change involves a process regarding the alteration of product codes associated with banking services, necessitating documentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Account Activation SOP">
  <data key="d0">Account Activation SOP</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Account Activation SOP is a Standard Operating Procedure that outlines the steps necessary for activating inoperative accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Due Diligence">
  <data key="d0">Customer Due Diligence</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer Due Diligence is a process initiated by bank officials to assess a customer's risk profile and verify their identity before account opening.&lt;SEP&gt;Customer Due Diligence is a process performed to verify the identity of clients and assess risk before engaging in transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Customer Due Diligence is the process of a bank verifying the identity and background of its clients to prevent financial crime.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Approval Committee">
  <data key="d0">Approval Committee</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Approval Committee is a group responsible for reviewing and approving significant banking decisions, such as account closures.&lt;SEP&gt;A governing body that establishes guidelines and policies for the handling of customer accounts within an organization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Individuals">
  <data key="d0">Individuals</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals are human beings capable of opening bank accounts either in single names or in joint capacities, with specified requirements for guardianship in certain cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minors">
  <data key="d0">Minors</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Minors are defined as individuals up to the age of 10 years who can have their savings or term deposit accounts opened by their natural guardians or court-appointed guardians.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Politically Exposed Persons">
  <data key="d0">Politically Exposed Persons</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Politically Exposed Persons (PEPs) are individuals who are entrusted with prominent public functions in foreign countries, impacting the due diligence required for their financial transactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FATCA">
  <data key="d0">FATCA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">FATCA stands for the Foreign Account Tax Compliance Act, requiring financial institutions to obtain tax residency status from customers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aadhaar">
  <data key="d0">Aadhaar</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Aadhaar is a unique identification number provided to Indian residents, which can be used for banking and customer verification processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Aadhaar is a unique identification number issued to residents of India based on their biometric and demographic data, often required as part of the KYC process for bank accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Natural Guardian">
  <data key="d0">Natural Guardian</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Natural Guardian refers to a parent or a legal guardian responsible for opening accounts on behalf of Minors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Court of Law">
  <data key="d0">Court of Law</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Court of Law is a legal entity that may appoint guardians to open accounts for Minors in the absence of a natural guardian.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Testamentary Guardian">
  <data key="d0">Testamentary Guardian</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Testamentary Guardian is someone appointed through a probated will to manage the financial affairs of a Minor.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minor Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Minor Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Minor accounts refer to bank accounts that can be opened for individuals below the age of 18, with specific requirements for account opening depending on the age of the minor.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sick Person">
  <data key="d0">Sick Person</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A sick person is defined as an individual who is unable to sign or be physically present in the bank due to health issues, which affects their ability to manage their bank account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blind Person">
  <data key="d0">Blind Person</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A blind person is an individual with significant visual impairment, who can open a bank account under specific regulations set by the bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visually Impaired Person">
  <data key="d0">Visually Impaired Person</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A visually impaired person is someone who has difficulty seeing but is not completely blind, and can also open bank accounts with no differential treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism">
  <data key="d0">National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">This organization is established under the Act for the Welfare of persons with disabilities, facilitating banking services for those with autism and related conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Account Opening Form">
  <data key="d0">Account Opening Form</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Account Opening Form is a document that must be filled out and signed by customers in order to establish a new bank account, with specific requirements based on the individual's circumstances.&lt;SEP&gt;The Account Opening Form is a document required by the bank for initiating the process of opening a new account and includes necessary details such as personal information and KYC documentation requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;The account opening form is a document that customers fill out to open an account, containing various fields for customer information.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-drawing-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FATCA Declaration Form">
  <data key="d0">FATCA Declaration Form</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A form that is signed by the guardian of a minor or incapacitated person, required for compliance with the Foreign Account Tax Compliance Act when opening a bank account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="District Courts">
  <data key="d0">District Courts</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">District Courts are legal authorities appointed under the Mental Health Act, 1987 to oversee the appointment of guardians for mentally ill persons.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Collectors of Districts">
  <data key="d0">Collectors of Districts</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Collectors of Districts are officials responsible for managing district affairs, including the appointment of guardians under the Mental Health Act, 1987.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Queer Partners">
  <data key="d0">Queer Partners</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals in a queer relationship who have the right to open joint bank accounts together.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Politically Exposed Person (PEP)">
  <data key="d0">Politically Exposed Person (PEP)</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals who are or have been entrusted with prominent public functions in a foreign country, requiring additional scrutiny in banking transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;A Politically Exposed Person (PEP) is an individual who holds a prominent public position or has a significant influence over a public entity and may be at higher risk for involvement in bribery or corruption.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-015</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unity Small Finance Bank Ltd.">
  <data key="d0">Unity Small Finance Bank Ltd.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Unity Small Finance Bank Ltd. is a financial institution that provides banking services, including accounts that can be opened under specific conditions such as KYC and managing customers' financial activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Unity Small Finance Bank Ltd. is a financial institution that provides banking services and is governed by regulations for specific client categories.&lt;SEP&gt;A financial institution providing various banking services, including staff benefits and account management.&lt;SEP&gt;Unity Small Finance Bank Ltd. is a financial institution offering various banking services, including account operation and management.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-013</data>
