<node id="Chief Business Officer">
  <data key="d0">Chief Business Officer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The executive in charge of business operations at Unity Small Finance Bank Ltd., who has the authority to make decisions regarding PEP accounts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Chief Business Officer is a senior executive responsible for overseeing business operations and customer relationships within Unity Small Finance Bank.&lt;SEP&gt;An official role representing the highest-ranking officer in the business management of an organization, involved in decision-making processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-021</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Branch Manager">
  <data key="d0">Branch Manager</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Branch Manager is the individual responsible for overseeing operations at a bank branch, including the management of staff and customer relations.&lt;SEP&gt;The individual responsible for managing a specific branch of Unity Small Finance Bank Ltd., including the recommendation of PEP account openings.&lt;SEP&gt;The Branch Manager is responsible for overseeing branch operations, including customer onboarding and compliance with banking procedures at Unity Small Finance Bank.&lt;SEP&gt;The individual responsible for overseeing the operations of a bank branch and approving customer profiles.&lt;SEP&gt;The Branch Manager oversees the branch operations at Unity Small Finance Bank and is responsible for managing customer relationships and staff.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Central AML Team">
  <data key="d0">Central AML Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Central AML Team is responsible for monitoring customer relationships and ensuring compliance with anti-money laundering regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Central AML Team is responsible for monitoring anti-money laundering practices and updating internal databases regarding customer risk ratings within Unity Small Finance Bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consumer Banking Team">
  <data key="d0">Consumer Banking Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Consumer Banking Team is part of Unity Small Finance Bank, tasked with handling customer requests and information related to banking activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Consumer Banking Team at Unity Small Finance Bank manages the current processes associated with account opening and related documentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-006</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CERSAI">
  <data key="d0">CERSAI</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CERSAI stands for the Central Registry of Securitisation Asset Reconstruction and Security Interest of India, which maintains records related to KYC and financial transactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KYC Identifier">
  <data key="d0">KYC Identifier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A KYC Identifier is a unique identification number that allows a bank to retrieve a customer's KYC records and verify their identity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OVD">
  <data key="d0">OVD</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">OVD stands for Official Valid Document, used as proof of identity or address in banking procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;OVD, or Official Valid Document, refers to a type of identification required for verification of identity and address.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Identification Number (CIF)">
  <data key="d0">Customer Identification Number (CIF)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer Identification Number (CIF) is a unique identifier created for each customer in the bank's Customer Relationship Management Solution, used for tracking customer profiles and banking activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Customer Identification Number is a unique identification assigned to customers, created during the KYC process for proper record-keeping in banking systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KYC">
  <data key="d0">KYC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">KYC, or Know Your Customer, is a process used by banks to verify the identity of their clients in order to prevent fraud and ensure compliance with legal requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Know Your Customer (KYC) is a process used by banks to verify the identity of their clients and assess potential risks in the relationship.&lt;SEP&gt;An abbreviation for Know Your Customer, a process used by financial institutions to verify the identity of their clients.&lt;SEP&gt;KYC, which stands for Know Your Customer, refers to the regulatory process that banks and financial institutions must follow to verify the identities of their clients, particularly focusing on accounts held by Politically Exposed Persons (PEPs).&lt;SEP&gt;Know Your Customer (KYC) is a compliance process that ensures financial institutions verify the identity and assess the risk of customers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-drawing-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-020</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BSBDA">
  <data key="d0">BSBDA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">BSBDA stands for Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account, a type of banking product in India that allows individuals to maintain a zero balance while also having restrictions on transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account (BSBDA) is a type of bank account that has no minimum balance requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PAN">
  <data key="d0">PAN</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">PAN, or Permanent Account Number, is a unique identifier issued by the Indian income tax department to individuals and businesses, required for various financial transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Permanent Account Number (PAN) is a unique identifier issued to individuals and entities for tax purposes in India.&lt;SEP&gt;PAN, or Permanent Account Number, is a unique identifier issued to individuals and entities for tax purposes in India.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Relationship Officer">
  <data key="d0">Relationship Officer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A Relationship Officer is a banking professional assigned to manage customer relations, ensuring satisfactory customer service and handling of accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Manager">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Manager</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Cluster Manager is a supervisory role within a banking framework responsible for managing multiple branches and ensuring they meet operational standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
