<node id="Zonal Manager">
  <data key="d0">Zonal Manager</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Zonal Manager oversees several branches within a specific geographic zone for the bank, responsible for regional performance and strategic decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KYC-AML Policy">
  <data key="d0">KYC-AML Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The KYC-AML Policy outlines the guidelines and procedures for Know Your Customer (KYC) and Anti-Money Laundering (AML) practices to prevent financial crimes and ensure compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;A set of guidelines established by the bank to prevent money laundering and ensure that customer identities are verified during the account opening process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BIDMS">
  <data key="d0">BIDMS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">BIDMS is an acronym for Banking Information and Data Management System, a platform used by the bank to store and manage customer data and documentation related to banking operations.&lt;SEP&gt;BIDMS refers to the Banking Identification and Data Management System used for processing customer identification and KYC data, especially for minors at Unity Small Finance Bank.&lt;SEP&gt;A Document Management System used by the bank for storing and retrieving customer KYC documents.&lt;SEP&gt;BIDMS is a feature or module within the software interface of Unity Small Finance Bank, indicated by an icon that is highlighted among other options.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-drawing-002</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OVDs">
  <data key="d0">OVDs</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">OVDs, or Official Valid Documents, refer to documents required for KYC purposes that establish the identity and address of the customer, ensuring verification in banking processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Self-Drawn Cheque">
  <data key="d0">Self-Drawn Cheque</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A Self-Drawn Cheque is a cheque drawn by an account holder on their own account as a means of making payments or deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786704170</data>
