The image displays a screenshot of a C-KYC (Customer Know Your Customer) data input form intended for banking or financial use. The top section indicates that the data is for office use only, showing fields for constitution type, account type, and customer number. The personal details section includes fields for the applicant's name, the father's and mother's names, date of birth, gender, PAN (Permanent Account Number), and proof of address. The form is designed for a minor, as indicated by the 'Name/title' field labeled 'Minor' and includes other information like first, middle, and last names, with specific inputs like 'MANAWA', 'KETAN', and 'PANDAV'. Overall, it appears to be part of a customer onboarding or verification process for a banking institution. The relationship with the leading text suggests that this form is part of a process that requires updating guardians' details and managing documents related to a minor applicant.</data>
