  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">[Table Name]inoperative_account_activation_sop_details

This table provides detailed descriptive guidelines regarding the activation of inoperative accounts and the necessary documents required for various banking procedures at Unity Small Finance Bank. The table contains multiple rows and columns, with information segmented into distinct categories related to account management and customer documentation requirements. The first data row discusses the procedures for activating accounts along with the requirement for KYC documents, indicating that a Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) is in place for activating inoperative accounts after fulfilling the KYC requirements. The second row outlines regulations pertaining to medium-risk customers, particularly the periodic update of KYC every eight years, as noted in a review by the Operational Risk Management Division (ORMD). Subsequent entries include detailed instructions on the documentation required for product code changes, emphasizing the importance of obtaining fresh operating instructions and KYC documents as account holders reach the age of majority. Additionally, there are stipulations for account closure procedures, including the necessity for approvals and defined repayment methods for significant closure amounts. Overall, the table serves as a comprehensive reference for the procedural aspects of managing inactive accounts and the requisite compliance measures, underscoring adherence to regulatory mandates issued by the Reserve Bank of India. The information reflects internal policies and implications for the handling of customer accounts, reinforcing guidelines established through the governance of the Approval Committee.

